    ^{:line 94 :tag atomic/Int32 :doc "Initialized from GOGC. GOGC=off means no GC.\n"} gcPercent









    ^{:line 104 :tag atomic/Int64 :doc "memoryLimit is the soft memory limit in bytes.\n\nInitialized from GOMEMLIMIT. GOMEMLIMIT=off is equivalent to MaxInt64\nwhich means no soft memory limit in practice.\n\nThis is an int64 instead of a uint64 to more easily maintain parity with\nthe SetMemoryLimit API, which sets a maximum at MaxInt64. This value\nshould never be negative.\n"} memoryLimit













    ^{:line 118 :tag uint64 :doc "heapMinimum is the minimum heap size at which to trigger GC.\nFor small heaps, this overrides the usual GOGC*live set rule.\n\nWhen there is a very small live set but a lot of allocation, simply\ncollecting when the heap reaches GOGC*live results in many GC\ncycles and high total per-GC overhead. This minimum amortizes this\nper-GC overhead while keeping the heap reasonably small.\n\nDuring initialization this is set to 4MB*GOGC/100. In the case of\nGOGC==0, this will set heapMinimum to 0, resulting in constant\ncollection even when the heap size is small, which is useful for\ndebugging.\n"} heapMinimum





    ^{:line 124 :tag atomic/Uint64 :doc "runway is the amount of runway in heap bytes allocated by the\napplication that we want to give the GC once it starts.\n\nThis is computed from consMark during mark termination.\n"} runway













    ^{:line 138 :tag float64 :doc "consMark is the estimated per-CPU consMark ratio for the application.\n\nIt represents the ratio between the application's allocation\nrate, as bytes allocated per CPU-time, and the GC's scan rate,\nas bytes scanned per CPU-time.\nThe units of this ratio are (B / cpu-ns) / (B / cpu-ns).\n\nAt a high level, this value is computed as the bytes of memory\nallocated (cons) per unit of scan work completed (mark) in a GC\ncycle, divided by the CPU time spent on each activity.\n\nUpdated at the end of each GC cycle, in endCycle.\n"} consMark




    ^{:line 143 :tag (array 4 float64) :doc "lastConsMark is the computed cons/mark value for the previous 4 GC\ncycles. Note that this is *not* the last value of consMark, but the\nmeasured cons/mark value in endCycle.\n"} lastConsMark





    ^{:line 149 :tag atomic/Uint64 :doc "gcPercentHeapGoal is the goal heapLive for when next GC ends derived\nfrom gcPercent.\n\nSet to ^uint64(0) if gcPercent is disabled.\n"} gcPercentHeapGoal












    ^{:line 162 :tag atomic/Uint64 :doc "sweepDistMinTrigger is the minimum trigger to ensure a minimum\nsweep distance.\n\nThis bound is also special because it applies to both the trigger\n*and* the goal (all other trigger bounds must be based *on* the goal).\n\nIt is computed ahead of time, at commit time. The theory is that,\nabsent a sudden change to a parameter like gcPercent, the trigger\nwill be chosen to always give the sweeper enough headroom. However,\nsuch a change might dramatically and suddenly move up the trigger,\nin which case we need to ensure the sweeper still has enough headroom.\n"} sweepDistMinTrigger





