    ^{:line 175 :tag uint64 :doc "lastHeapGoal is the value of heapGoal at the moment the last GC\nended. Note that this is distinct from the last value heapGoal had,\nbecause it could change if e.g. gcPercent changes.\n\nRead and written with the world stopped or with mheap_.lock held.\n"} lastHeapGoal




















    ^{:line 196 :tag atomic/Uint64 :doc "heapLive is the number of bytes considered live by the GC.\nThat is: retained by the most recent GC plus allocated\nsince then. heapLive ≤ memstats.totalAlloc-memstats.totalFree, since\nheapAlloc includes unmarked objects that have not yet been swept (and\nhence goes up as we allocate and down as we sweep) while heapLive\nexcludes these objects (and hence only goes up between GCs).\n\nTo reduce contention, this is updated only when obtaining a span\nfrom an mcentral and at this point it counts all of the unallocated\nslots in that span (which will be allocated before that mcache\nobtains another span from that mcentral). Hence, it slightly\noverestimates the \"true\" live heap size. It's better to overestimate\nthan to underestimate because 1) this triggers the GC earlier than\nnecessary rather than potentially too late and 2) this leads to a\nconservative GC rate rather than a GC rate that is potentially too\nlow.\n\nWhenever this is updated, call traceHeapAlloc() and\nthis gcControllerState's revise() method.\n"} heapLive







    ^{:line 204 :tag atomic/Uint64 :doc "heapScan is the number of bytes of \"scannable\" heap. This is the\nlive heap (as counted by heapLive), but omitting no-scan objects and\nno-scan tails of objects.\n\nThis value is fixed at the start of a GC cycle. It represents the\nmaximum scannable heap.\n"} heapScan






